  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Sensor Data Fusion and Kalman Filtering Demo with MADA Convergence Monitoring\n",
        "\n",
        "This interactive Jupyter notebook demonstrates sensor data fusion using an Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) for drone navigation. It integrates data from IMUs (accelerometer, gyroscope), GPS, altimeter, magnetometer, **and Hall sensors for MADA convergence monitoring**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Key components:\n",
        "- KalmanFilter Class: Fuses sensor data for position, velocity, and attitude estimation.\n",
        "- Sensor Simulation: Generates noisy sensor readings to mimic real-world data.\n",
        "- **MADA Convergence Tracking**: Monitors magnetic field alignment quality in real-time.\n",
        "- Visualization: Plots true vs. fused states over time, plus convergence quality.\n",
        "\n",
        "**CRITICAL**: This demo shows how to detect magnetic field misalignment that would prevent QED vacuum polarization propulsion.\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the cells sequentially to see the demo. Adjust parameters like noise levels or simulation steps for experimentation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import sys\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from matplotlib.patches import Rectangle\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add parent directory to path for imports\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.getcwd()), '..'))\n",
        "\n",
        "from ai.navigation import KalmanFilter, simulate_sensors\n",
        "from simulations.equations import calculate_convergence_quality, CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL, CONVERGENCE_WARNING, CONVERGENCE_CRITICAL\n",
        "\n",
        "# Simulation parameters\n",
        "DT = 0.1  # Time step (s)\n",
        "NUM_STEPS = 100  # Number of simulation steps\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initial true state\n",
        "true_pos = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.0])\n",
        "true_vel = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.0])\n",
        "true_att = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.0])  # Roll, pitch, yaw\n",
        "\n",
        "# Arrays to store histories\n",
        "true_pos_history = [true_pos.copy()]\n",
        "fused_pos_history = []\n",
        "true_vel_history = [true_vel.copy()]\n",
        "fused_vel_history = []\n",
        "\n",
        "# NEW: MADA convergence tracking\n",
        "B1_history = []  # MADA unit 1 field vectors\n",
        "B2_history = []  # MADA unit 2 field vectors\n",
        "convergence_history = []  # Convergence quality over time\n",
        "convergence_warnings = []  # Warning events\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize Kalman Filter\n",
        "kf = KalmanFilter(dt=DT)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Sensor Fusion Demo Initialized\")\n",
        "print(f\"Simulation: {NUM_STEPS} steps at {DT}s intervals ({NUM_STEPS * DT}s total)\")\n",
        "print(\"MADA convergence monitoring: ENABLED\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Simulated MADA Hall Sensor Class\n",
        "\n",
        "This class simulates Hall sensors that measure magnetic field vectors from both MADA units. In a real system, these would be 3-axis Hall sensors positioned at each MADA unit.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key Feature**: Can inject misalignment at specific time steps to demonstrate detection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class SimulatedMADAHallSensors:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Simulates Hall sensors for MADA convergence monitoring.\n",
        "    By default, fields are properly converging (opposing).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, B_magnitude=50.0, noise_level=0.5, mada1_pos=(-0.3, 0, 0), mada2_pos=(0.3, 0, 0)):\n",
        "        self.B_magnitude = B_magnitude\n",
        "        self.noise_level = noise_level\n",
        "        self.mada1_pos = np.array(mada1_pos)\n",
        "        self.mada2_pos = np.array(mada2_pos)\n",
        "        self.center = np.array([0, 0, 0])\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Calculate nominal directions (converging toward center)\n",
        "        self.B1_nominal_dir = (self.center - self.mada1_pos) / np.linalg.norm(self.center - self.mada1_pos)\n",
        "        self.B2_nominal_dir = (self.center - self.mada2_pos) / np.linalg.norm(self.center - self.mada2_pos)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Current directions (can be modified to inject faults)\n",
        "        self.B1_current_dir = self.B1_nominal_dir.copy()\n",
        "        self.B2_current_dir = self.B2_nominal_dir.copy()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.misalignment_active = False\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def read_mada1_field(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Read magnetic field vector from MADA unit 1 (with noise).\"\"\"\n",
        "        noise = np.random.normal(0, self.noise_level, 3)\n",
        "        B1 = self.B1_current_dir * self.B_magnitude + noise\n",
        "        return B1\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def read_mada2_field(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Read magnetic field vector from MADA unit 2 (with noise).\"\"\"\n",
        "        noise = np.random.normal(0, self.noise_level, 3)\n",
        "        B2 = self.B2_current_dir * self.B_magnitude + noise\n",
        "        return B2\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def inject_misalignment(self, angle_deg, axis='z'):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Inject a misalignment fault by rotating MADA2 field direction.\n",
        "        Simulates mechanical shift, magnet demagnetization, or wiring error.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        angle_rad = np.deg2rad(angle_deg)\n",
        "        if axis == 'z':\n",
        "            rotation_matrix = np.array([\n",
        "                [np.cos(angle_rad), -np.sin(angle_rad), 0],\n",
        "                [np.sin(angle_rad), np.cos(angle_rad), 0],\n",
        "                [0, 0, 1]\n",
        "            ])\n",
        "        # Add other axes if needed\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.B2_current_dir = rotation_matrix @ self.B2_nominal_dir\n",
        "        self.misalignment_active = True\n",
        "        print(f\"⚠️  FAULT INJECTED: {angle_deg}° misalignment on MADA unit 2\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def inject_divergence(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Inject critical fault: both fields pointing away (the FreeCAD bug!).\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        self.B1_current_dir = -self.B1_nominal_dir  # Reverse direction\n",
        "        self.B2_current_dir = -self.B2_nominal_dir\n",
        "        self.misalignment_active = True\n",
        "        print(f\"🔴 CRITICAL FAULT INJECTED: Diverging fields (FreeCAD configuration error!)\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def reset(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Reset to nominal converging configuration.\"\"\"\n",
        "        self.B1_current_dir = self.B1_nominal_dir.copy()\n",
        "        self.B2_current_dir = self.B2_nominal_dir.copy()\n",
        "        self.misalignment_active = False\n",
        "        print(\"✓ Hall sensors reset to nominal configuration\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize Hall sensors\n",
        "hall_sensors = SimulatedMADAHallSensors(B_magnitude=50.0, noise_level=0.5)\n",
        "print(\"\\nHall Sensors initialized:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  MADA 1 position: {hall_sensors.mada1_pos}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  MADA 2 position: {hall_sensors.mada2_pos}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Nominal field strength: {hall_sensors.B_magnitude} T\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Simulation Loop with MADA Monitoring\n",
        "\n",
        "In this cell, we simulate drone motion with constant acceleration. At each step:\n",
        "1. Update true state.\n",
        "2. Simulate noisy sensor readings (IMU, GPS, etc.).\n",
        "3. **Read Hall sensors for MADA field vectors**.\n",
        "4. **Calculate convergence quality**.\n",
        "5. Predict with IMU data.\n",
        "6. Update with GPS/altimeter/magnetometer data.\n",
        "7. Store fused estimates and convergence data.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Fault Injection**: At step 50, we inject a 30° misalignment to demonstrate detection.\n",
        "At step 75, we inject a critical divergence fault."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Simulated constant acceleration (e.g., forward thrust)\n",
        "true_accel = np.array([0.5, 0.0, 0.0])  # m/s²\n",
        "true_gyro = np.array([0.0, 0.01, 0.0])  # rad/s (small yaw)\n",
        "\n",
        "fault_injected_at_step = None\n",
        "critical_fault_at_step = None\n",
        "\n",
        "for step in range(NUM_STEPS):\n",
        "    # Inject faults at specific steps for demonstration\n",
        "    if step == 50:\n",
        "        hall_sensors.inject_misalignment(30)  # 30° misalignment\n",
        "        fault_injected_at_step = step\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if step == 75:\n",
        "        hall_sensors.inject_divergence()  # Critical fault\n",
        "        critical_fault_at_step = step\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Update true state\n",
        "    true_vel += true_accel * DT\n",
        "    true_pos += true_vel * DT\n",
        "    true_att += true_gyro * DT\n",
        "    true_att = np.mod(true_att + np.pi, 2 * np.pi) - np.pi  # Normalize angles\n",
        "    \n",
        "    true_pos_history.append(true_pos.copy())\n",
        "    true_vel_history.append(true_vel.copy())\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Simulate sensors (with noise)\n",
        "    imu_accel, imu_gyro, gps_pos, gps_vel, alt_z, mag_att = simulate_sensors(true_pos, true_vel, true_att)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # NEW: Read Hall sensors for MADA convergence\n",
        "    B1 = hall_sensors.read_mada1_field()\n",
        "    B2 = hall_sensors.read_mada2_field()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Calculate convergence quality\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        convergence_quality = calculate_convergence_quality(B1, B2)\n",
        "    except ValueError:\n",
        "        convergence_quality = 0.0\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Store MADA data\n",
        "    B1_history.append(B1.copy())\n",
        "    B2_history.append(B2.copy())\n",
        "    convergence_history.append(convergence_quality)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Check for convergence warnings\n",
        "    if convergence_quality < CONVERGENCE_CRITICAL:\n",
        "        convergence_warnings.append((step, convergence_quality, 'CRITICAL'))\n",
        "        if step >= 75:  # Only print after critical fault injection\n",
        "            print(f\"Step {step}: 🔴 CRITICAL - Convergence quality = {convergence_quality:.3f}\")\n",
        "    elif convergence_quality < CONVERGENCE_WARNING:\n",
        "        convergence_warnings.append((step, convergence_quality, 'WARNING'))\n",
        "        if step == 50:  # Print at first fault\n",
        "            print(f\"Step {step}: ⚠️  WARNING - Convergence quality = {convergence_quality:.3f}\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Kalman predict and update\n",
        "    kf.predict(imu_accel, imu_gyro)\n",
        "    measurements = np.concatenate([gps_pos, gps_vel, mag_att, [alt_z]])\n",
        "    kf.update(measurements)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    fused_pos_history.append(kf.x[0:3].copy())\n",
        "    fused_vel_history.append(kf.x[3:6].copy())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert histories to arrays for plotting\n",
        "true_pos_history = np.array(true_pos_history)\n",
        "fused_pos_history = np.array(fused_pos_history)\n",
        "true_vel_history = np.array(true_vel_history)\n",
        "fused_vel_history = np.array(fused_vel_history)\n",
        "B1_history = np.array(B1_history)\n",
        "B2_history = np.array(B2_history)\n",
        "convergence_history = np.array(convergence_history)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\n✓ Simulation complete: {NUM_STEPS} steps\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Convergence warnings: {len(convergence_warnings)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Mean convergence quality: {np.mean(convergence_history):.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Min convergence quality: {np.min(convergence_history):.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## NEW: MADA Convergence Quality Plot\n",
        "\n",
        "This plot shows convergence quality over time with threshold indicators.\n",
        "- **Green zone** (≥0.95): Optimal operation\n",
        "- **Yellow zone** (0.85-0.95): Acceptable but monitor\n",
        "- **Orange zone** (0.80-0.85): Warning - reduce thrust\n",
        "- **Red zone** (<0.80): Critical - emergency landing required"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "time_steps_mada = np.arange(0, NUM_STEPS * DT, DT)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot convergence quality\n",
        "ax.plot(time_steps_mada, convergence_history, color='black', linewidth=2, label='Convergence Quality')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add threshold lines\n",
        "ax.axhline(y=CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL, color='green', linestyle='--', linewidth=1, label='Optimal (0.95)')\n",
        "ax.axhline(y=CONVERGENCE_WARNING, color='orange', linestyle='--', linewidth=1, label='Warning (0.85)')\n",
        "ax.axhline(y=CONVERGENCE_CRITICAL, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=1, label='Critical (0.80)')\n",
        "ax.axhline(y=0, color='gray', linestyle=':', linewidth=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add colored zones\n",
        "ax.axhspan(CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL, 1.1, alpha=0.1, color='green', label='Optimal Zone')\n",
        "ax.axhspan(CONVERGENCE_WARNING, CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL, alpha=0.1, color='yellow')\n",
        "ax.axhspan(CONVERGENCE_CRITICAL, CONVERGENCE_WARNING, alpha=0.1, color='orange')\n",
        "ax.axhspan(-1.1, CONVERGENCE_CRITICAL, alpha=0.1, color='red', label='Critical Zone')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Mark fault injection points\n",
        "if fault_injected_at_step is not None:\n",
        "    ax.axvline(x=fault_injected_at_step * DT, color='orange', linestyle=':', linewidth=2, alpha=0.7)\n",
        "    ax.text(fault_injected_at_step * DT, 0.5, '30° Misalignment\\nInjected', \n",
        "            rotation=90, verticalalignment='bottom', fontsize=9)\n",
        "\n",
        "if critical_fault_at_step is not None:\n",
        "    ax.axvline(x=critical_fault_at_step * DT, color='red', linestyle=':', linewidth=2, alpha=0.7)\n",
        "    ax.text(critical_fault_at_step * DT, 0.5, 'Diverging Fields\\nInjected', \n",
        "            rotation=90, verticalalignment='bottom', fontsize=9)\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel('Time (s)', fontsize=12)\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel('Convergence Quality', fontsize=12)\n",
        "ax.set_title('MADA Magnetic Field Convergence Quality Over Time', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
        "ax.set_ylim([-1.1, 1.1])\n",
        "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "ax.legend(loc='lower left', fontsize=9)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nKey Observations:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Steps 0-49: Convergence quality ≈ {np.mean(convergence_history[:50]):.3f} (OPTIMAL)\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Steps 50-74: Quality ≈ {np.mean(convergence_history[50:75]):.3f} after 30° misalignment (WARNING)\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Steps 75-99: Quality ≈ {np.mean(convergence_history[75:]):.3f} after divergence (CRITICAL)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## NEW: MADA Field Vector Magnitude Plot\n",
